  "id": "COMPOUND:295 - PROTEIN:5292",
  "verbalization": "Mitomycin is linked to NCI-H1694 through a series of target relationships, with the most direct pathway involving Bromodomain-containing protein 4. This protein is targeted by palmarumycin CP18, which in turn targets NCI-H1694. The second pathway connects mitomycin to Lysine-specific demethylase 4C, which is targeted by a compound that also targets NCI-H1694. The third pathway links mitomycin to TE-9, which is targeted by the same compound that targets NCI-H1694. These findings suggest that mitomycin may exert its effects through multiple pathways, all of which ultimately engage NCI-H1694 as a downstream target. The shared involvement of compounds that target NCI-H1694 across different pathways implies a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of epigenetic or chromatin-related processes. The evidence supports a role for mitomycin in influencing NCI-H1694 through diverse molecular mechanisms, though the exact nature of these interactions remains to be fully elucidated.",
